1
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:13,360
Try lightening up and stepping away.

2
00:00:20,740 --> 00:00:26,880
Toward the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

3
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:33,980
kick a pebble and even your shoes go flying.

4
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:42,240
So, to the carpenter boss
who had been saving up,

5
00:00:42,690 --> 00:00:48,440
they laughed that I'm still just a kid.

6
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:53,560
Even if I chase after some energy somewhere,

7
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:58,640
Katsushika, a little saving up,
one yawn, nothing changes.

8
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:02,540
The streets feel strangely gentle.

9
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:10,520
From the pointed hat and the water bottle,

10
00:01:10,520 --> 00:01:16,780
great stone, heavenly origin, the sun sets.

11
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow will end just like this, won't it.

12
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:30,380
Hey, Katsushika Shibamata,
even happiness gets lost.

13
00:01:30,380 --> 00:01:33,880
I only realized it because I'm such a fool.

14
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:40,860
Ryo-san, getting smaller!

15
00:02:16,820 --> 00:02:17,680
My stomach!

16
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:19,460
Divine punishment!

17
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:22,900
Divine punishment, right on the spot!

18
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:24,900
Whoa! That's seriously infuriating!

19
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:26,640
If my boyfriend did something like that!

20
00:02:26,860 --> 00:02:27,540
Divine punishment!

21
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:32,420
Divine punishment, right on the spot!

22
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:35,080
Divine punishment!

23
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:39,820
Divine punishment, right on the spot!

24
00:02:47,580 --> 00:02:49,100
Chief Hanayama of Public Safety

25
00:02:57,740 --> 00:03:02,640
Divine punishment! Divine punishment! Divine
punishment! Divine punishment! Divine punishment!

26
00:03:03,020 --> 00:03:10,320
I'll smite you with divine punishment!

27
00:03:11,420 --> 00:03:12,580
Splendid!

28
00:03:12,580 --> 00:03:13,560
Good morning.

29
00:03:14,180 --> 00:03:18,120
General, the peace of the
mortal world is in our hands.

30
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:20,680
Not taking our eyes off it for a moment.

31
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:26,440
A suspicious-looking man.

32
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:30,600
Whoever's it is, I'll take it.

33
00:03:32,860 --> 00:03:34,080
Let go, you fool!

34
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:35,380
Divine punishment!

35
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:38,620
Ow

36
00:03:38,620 --> 00:03:39,960
Divine punishment can't touch me!

37
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:41,540
What's wrong, Ryo-chan?

38
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,700
My stomach hurts so bad I can't stand it.

39
00:03:45,540 --> 00:03:47,860
Oh no, Ryo-chan, did you eat this?

40
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:50,040
This sushi is from a week ago!

41
00:03:50,040 --> 00:03:52,060
Don't save any of it.

42
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:56,780
Score! This gives me a
good excuse to skip work.

43
00:03:56,780 --> 00:03:59,160
I'm leaving early.

44
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:03,100
Go to the main station and have them
send something nutritious to my home.

45
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:04,160
Got it.

46
00:04:06,380 --> 00:04:08,040
Using divine punishment like that...

47
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:09,120
What a man!

48
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:11,320
It's me, Kenwasa!

49
00:04:11,540 --> 00:04:13,740
My stomach's calmed down quite a bit.

50
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:16,180
Here it comes!

51
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:18,640
It's coming out!

52
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:29,600
Saved.

53
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:31,940
It's too early to relax!

54
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:33,060
Kenwasa!

55
00:04:35,420 --> 00:04:39,200
My hair's gone!

56
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:41,100
Tsuyamuchō!

57
00:04:41,860 --> 00:04:43,900
I'm going to take a bath later anyway.

58
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:46,460
Once I got that stuff out,
I felt completely better.

59
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:47,580
Gross stuff.

60
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:50,660
Hey! They said they'd show me the Meimuro!

61
00:04:50,840 --> 00:05:01,940
My little plastic model!

62
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:07,360
Isn't this the one I bought at
the clearance sale for 100 yen?

63
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:08,400
Gaanaa...

64
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:21,140
Senpai, are you all right? I heard Honda had stomach trouble,
so I brought you some rice porridge...

65
00:05:21,140 --> 00:05:23,620
(unintelligible)

66
00:05:23,620 --> 00:05:24,340
It's the theme!

67
00:05:27,020 --> 00:05:31,980
Theme, how lovely!

68
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:33,800
Hey! It flew off!

69
00:05:34,340 --> 00:05:35,820
S-sorry!

70
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:38,140
This is the plan from before.

71
00:05:39,260 --> 00:05:39,420
Yeah.

72
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:42,360
It's crushed!

73
00:05:42,720 --> 00:05:44,440
S-sorry, senpai!

74
00:05:44,940 --> 00:05:48,280
Pay for it! Make good on it!
This cost 50,000 yen, you know!

75
00:05:48,660 --> 00:05:49,820
W-what, 50,000!?

76
00:05:49,820 --> 00:05:51,920
That's right, 50,000 yen.

77
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:54,460
Please do it, won't you?

78
00:05:54,460 --> 00:05:57,420
Making a fortune off a 100-yen model kit!

79
00:05:58,720 --> 00:05:59,640
You liar!

80
00:05:59,640 --> 00:06:00,580
Swindler, con artist!

81
00:06:00,580 --> 00:06:02,740
Divine punishment!
Divine punishment! Divine punishment!

82
00:06:02,740 --> 00:06:03,580
Divine punishment!

83
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:07,360
Chief Hanayama!

84
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:09,280
No matter how much divine
punishment I give this man,

85
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:10,220
he shows no sign of learning his lesson.

86
00:06:10,220 --> 00:06:12,600
This wretched scoundrel!

87
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:13,820
I won't let this stand!

88
00:06:13,820 --> 00:06:16,080
In the name of the Chief of
Lower World Public Safety,

89
00:06:16,760 --> 00:06:18,140
I, Hanayama,

90
00:06:18,140 --> 00:06:19,480
shall punish you!

91
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:26,620
That feels much better.

92
00:06:30,980 --> 00:06:34,340
What is it, old man? Are you lost?
Forgot where your home is?

93
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:37,420
I am Hanayama, who has come from heaven.

94
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:39,440
You didn't come from there,
you're about to go there, right?

95
00:06:39,520 --> 00:06:40,560
Hah, move aside, move aside.

96
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:42,120
What's that noise!

97
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:44,985
I'm busy right now, so another time,

98
00:06:45,035 --> 00:06:47,660
come back when I'm so
bored I'm about to die.

99
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:51,634
I came from heaven to make
you a decent human being,

100
00:06:51,684 --> 00:06:53,120
the great Chief of Public Order!

101
00:06:53,380 --> 00:06:53,960
Yeah, yeah.

102
00:06:55,740 --> 00:07:00,560
To make you into a decent person, I came from
heaven as the Chief of Public Order, naruhodo.

103
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:02,820
That's exactly the same, you know!

104
00:07:08,140 --> 00:07:11,580
Damn you, this one's even more fun!

105
00:07:13,300 --> 00:07:13,920
Hey,

106
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:14,980
Ahahahaha!

107
00:07:17,320 --> 00:07:18,540
I won't forgive you!

108
00:07:18,740 --> 00:07:20,520
Go to the path where justice stands!

109
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:21,880
Divine punishment, nya!

110
00:07:25,480 --> 00:07:26,400
How's that, me?

111
00:07:27,260 --> 00:07:29,800
I've turned into a child!

112
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:31,480
Fuwahahaha!

113
00:07:31,900 --> 00:07:34,820
With that body,
I'll recall my pure childhood heart

114
00:07:34,860 --> 00:07:38,100
and reflect on my past deeds and be reborn!

115
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:39,060
Lucky!

116
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:39,580
What?

117
00:07:39,580 --> 00:07:43,380
Now the bus, train,
and movies are all child fares!

118
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:46,960
And as a kid, I can play all day
long without anyone scolding me.

119
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:48,500
It's like a dream!

120
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:50,400
Thanks, old man.

121
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:52,640
You brat, how dare you say such a thing!

122
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:56,460
Poop, wee-wee, poop, wee-wee!

123
00:07:57,340 --> 00:07:59,400
Oyama Amusement Park!

124
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:00,860
Surprising, surprising!

125
00:08:00,860 --> 00:08:03,280
Plump, bouncing butt!

126
00:08:03,280 --> 00:08:06,260
Datchuno, datchuno!

127
00:08:07,380 --> 00:08:09,000
Still going at it, old man?

128
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:11,460
Maybe you shouldn't overdo it?

129
00:08:11,740 --> 00:08:13,860
This time, I will never forgive you!

130
00:08:13,940 --> 00:08:17,280
I don't want to give you something
even harsher as a greeting!

131
00:08:17,440 --> 00:08:18,960
Lightning Special!

132
00:08:23,340 --> 00:08:25,760
So, this time you're really beaten,
aren't you?

133
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:26,780
Serves you right!

134
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:29,180
Nyah, nyah, spank your bottom!

135
00:08:29,180 --> 00:08:30,000
Dachūno

136
00:08:30,510 --> 00:08:31,440
Dachūno?

137
00:08:32,180 --> 00:08:34,760
Chief Hanayama is falling apart.

138
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:36,760
Mountain Amusement Park

139
00:08:40,260 --> 00:08:41,500
I'm back.

140
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:43,700
Senpai

141
00:08:44,220 --> 00:08:45,200
Ryo-san

142
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:49,160
I don't have one.

143
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:52,200
Ryo-san's off gallivanting somewhere again

144
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:53,920
Honestly, how outrageous.

145
00:08:55,020 --> 00:08:56,580
Did you just say something?

146
00:08:56,580 --> 00:08:57,340
No, sir.

147
00:08:57,340 --> 00:08:58,400
Must've been my imagination.

148
00:08:59,500 --> 00:08:59,980
What?

149
00:08:59,980 --> 00:09:02,000
No, we didn't say anything.

150
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:02,920
We didn't say a word.

151
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:05,600
That's strange, I could've sworn I heard

152
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:08,200
Hey, I'm right here! I'm right here!

153
00:09:13,580 --> 00:09:15,020
It sounded like Ryotsu's voice, but...

154
00:09:15,020 --> 00:09:16,960
I wonder if he's hiding somewhere.

155
00:09:19,280 --> 00:09:21,200
Chief, there's a weird bug on your shoulder!

156
00:09:23,100 --> 00:09:25,820
I'm sure I just heard Reiko's voice...

157
00:09:25,820 --> 00:09:27,820
I'm right here! Right here!

158
00:09:28,420 --> 00:09:29,280
Good morning.

159
00:09:32,060 --> 00:09:34,440
What's with you three? How lewd!

160
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:36,040
Staring at people's legs like that...

161
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:39,060
No, it's not like that, Reiko!
It's under your legs -

162
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:41,560
Ryotsu!

163
00:09:41,560 --> 00:09:42,040
Yoisho!

164
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:47,120
W-what are you doing?

165
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:47,940
I don't know!

166
00:09:48,020 --> 00:09:51,440
Some weird old man showed up and cast
some kind of spell on him before leaving!

167
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:52,300
Magic?

168
00:09:52,520 --> 00:09:54,920
Just put me down already, Chief.

169
00:09:54,920 --> 00:09:55,960
O-okay.

170
00:09:57,320 --> 00:10:00,000
I can't believe something like
this is actually happening.

171
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,800
It's like a magical girl anime.

172
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:03,740
But he's tiny and cute, isn't he?

173
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:05,020
What are you saying!

174
00:10:05,300 --> 00:10:06,480
Spare a thought for my side too...

175
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:07,000
Ocha-a!

176
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:09,760
Don't just carelessly set
things down on the desk!

177
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:13,300
I'm not taking him off your hands anymore!

178
00:10:13,560 --> 00:10:14,260
Ryo-san!

179
00:10:15,220 --> 00:10:17,380
But how do we eat this?

180
00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:20,180
If it's food, I'll feed him myself.

181
00:10:20,180 --> 00:10:22,500
Hey! Don't treat me like a pet!

182
00:10:22,860 --> 00:10:24,060
Sorry, I just did it without thinking!

183
00:10:24,260 --> 00:10:26,840
Blow, blow, there, open wide.

184
00:10:26,840 --> 00:10:29,020
Mm

185
00:10:29,020 --> 00:10:31,340
Hot, hot, hot, hot, hot, hot, hot!

186
00:10:31,340 --> 00:10:34,100
Sorry, sweetie-pie, was it too hot?

187
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:37,040
What's with that tone you'd use with a pet!

188
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:38,700
Sorry, I just did it without thinking.

189
00:10:39,140 --> 00:10:42,460
Reiko, you're on duty.
Get back to work, get back to work.

190
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:43,020
Yes, sir.

191
00:10:43,260 --> 00:10:45,040
Then what about food? What about my food?

192
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:49,100
Don't be spoiled!
Take care of yourself. Everyone's busy.

193
00:10:49,540 --> 00:10:50,420
We've got some.

194
00:10:51,460 --> 00:10:53,383
This

195
00:10:53,433 --> 00:10:57,380
It's like the crater of a volcano.

196
00:10:57,960 --> 00:10:59,740
We'd better wait until it cools down.

197
00:11:00,020 --> 00:11:00,380
Ryotsu.

198
00:11:00,520 --> 00:11:01,920
Whoa, hot, whoa, hot!

199
00:11:03,180 --> 00:11:03,980
Whoa, eek.

200
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:05,180
Gu-chee.

201
00:11:05,180 --> 00:11:05,900
Nooo!

202
00:11:06,300 --> 00:11:07,780
Chief, your tea is ready...

203
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:09,160
Whoa!

204
00:11:10,940 --> 00:11:12,140
Achoo!

205
00:11:13,260 --> 00:11:13,560
How is it?

206
00:11:13,880 --> 00:11:16,580
Whoa! It's hot! Ken-chan, take it off!

207
00:11:16,700 --> 00:11:17,400
W-what... is it gonna fly?

208
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:18,840
Take it! Hurry, take it off!

209
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:21,340
Excuse us.

210
00:11:23,160 --> 00:11:24,340
That was a rough ordeal.

211
00:11:24,820 --> 00:11:26,180
Ryotsu, got a minute?

212
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:27,120
What is it?

213
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:29,140
Could you do me a favor and take on a job?

214
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:29,820
A job?

215
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:34,220
I need you to get a 500-yen coin that
fell into the gap behind the locker.

216
00:11:35,380 --> 00:11:37,220
Why should I do something like that?

217
00:11:37,220 --> 00:11:38,260
Just go.

218
00:11:38,260 --> 00:11:43,260
Searching for lost items is a
proper duty for a police officer.

219
00:11:43,260 --> 00:11:44,520
Fine, fine.

220
00:11:44,520 --> 00:11:45,700
Guess I'll go, then.

221
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:48,260
How huge it is!

222
00:11:49,280 --> 00:11:50,140
Damn it!

223
00:11:51,100 --> 00:11:53,120
This heavy 500-yen coin!

224
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:57,660
Thanks for your hard work, then.

225
00:11:57,660 --> 00:11:59,440
This is money I found, so it's mine.

226
00:11:59,440 --> 00:12:00,620
I'll take a 10% cut.

227
00:12:00,620 --> 00:12:01,460
10%.

228
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:02,760
Heavy.

229
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:03,780
It's heavy.

230
00:12:04,420 --> 00:12:07,580
Even though you've shrunk,
your greed hasn't changed one bit.

231
00:12:07,580 --> 00:12:10,980
Senpai, even though you've gotten smaller,
you seem like you'll survive just fine.

232
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:15,900
You know, this could actually be
a pretty good way to make money.

233
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:28,720
I'd like you to paint
this 1/36 scale figure.

234
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:31,120
So that's three figures to paint

235
00:12:32,760 --> 00:12:39,500
That'll be 3,000 yen up front. Senpai, you're the only one
in the world who can give those tiny dolls facial expressions.

236
00:12:39,500 --> 00:12:47,460
Typical Ryo-san, starting a business right away just because you've shrunk.
I've got a fish bone stuck in my throat and I can't get it out.

237
00:12:47,460 --> 00:12:52,500
I wish my Mii-chan would
take some of this too.

238
00:12:53,500 --> 00:13:01,440
I can't get the thread through the needle... Booming business, booming business!
If we're making this much in just a few hours, it's not bad at all.

239
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:11,400
As always, you're a greedy one, Senpai. And with your size,
your tableware only needs to be about a hundredth of the usual, and you don't have to pay rent either.

240
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:17,320
How enviable!
Senpai, I bought you the Mii-chan House.

241
00:13:18,320 --> 00:13:21,640
I've been waiting.
Hurry up and show me my new house.

242
00:13:21,820 --> 00:13:22,140
Yes.

243
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:28,640
How nostalgic. I used to play
with these all the time as a kid.

244
00:13:28,940 --> 00:13:32,440
The girlish taste bothers me a bit, but well,
it's pretty luxurious and not bad at all.

245
00:13:32,820 --> 00:13:34,320
Even this is big enough, isn't it.

246
00:13:36,080 --> 00:13:38,380
Senpai, the bath is ready.

247
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:42,840
How's the water temperature?

248
00:13:43,120 --> 00:13:43,960
It's just right.

249
00:13:44,340 --> 00:13:47,020
You look just like Medama-Oyaji
from GeGeGe no Kitaro.

250
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:50,300
Yes, that side's perfect too.

251
00:13:50,300 --> 00:13:55,100
I gathered nothing but your favorite samples
from the high-end Dokkaat tasting selection.

252
00:13:55,660 --> 00:13:56,420
Good work.

253
00:13:57,380 --> 00:14:00,980
I'll deduct your pay from the cost of
that plastic model the other day, got it?

254
00:14:00,980 --> 00:14:02,220
Yes, thank you very much.

255
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:05,280
Well then, everyone, excuse me.

256
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:07,400
Thanks for your hard work.

257
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:09,000
Right, then.

258
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:10,760
Well then, let's eat.

259
00:14:12,860 --> 00:14:15,540
He's living a far more
luxurious life than my place.

260
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:18,920
Chief!

261
00:14:19,680 --> 00:14:21,800
Ryotsu! What is this?!

262
00:14:22,480 --> 00:14:24,600
Well, just a part-time job...

263
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:29,160
A part-time job? You complete idiot!

264
00:14:29,880 --> 00:14:31,860
Don't you dare take
advantage of being small!

265
00:14:32,180 --> 00:14:34,680
Properly fulfill your
duties as a police officer!

266
00:14:35,160 --> 00:14:35,820
Yes, sir.

267
00:14:36,260 --> 00:14:40,460
And all of you, don't spoil Ryotsu! Treat
him as a full-fledged officer! Understood?

268
00:14:40,680 --> 00:14:41,260
Yes!

269
00:14:41,560 --> 00:14:42,400
Well

270
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:43,480
Is it around here?

271
00:14:43,580 --> 00:14:44,100
Yeah, that's right.

272
00:14:48,660 --> 00:14:51,040
Nakagawa, it's the phone, the phone!

273
00:14:51,300 --> 00:14:52,680
You answer it, Ryotsu!

274
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:56,920
Don't be unreasonable.
How could I possibly answer it?

275
00:14:57,280 --> 00:14:58,460
Just hurry up and answer it!

276
00:14:59,460 --> 00:15:02,360
Fine, fine. I'll answer it, all right.

277
00:15:03,180 --> 00:15:04,500
One, two, three.

278
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:06,500
Wh-, right away!

279
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:34,820
Mmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm...

280
00:15:37,560 --> 00:15:40,860
The culprit failed to rob the cash
transport truck from Kameari Bank.

281
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:46,060
The suspect is currently believed to be holding
hostages at Yamazaki Store in Kameari 3-chome.

282
00:15:51,500 --> 00:15:52,140
What's the situation?

283
00:15:53,180 --> 00:15:58,040
The suspect seems to be holding a university student
from the boarding house on the second floor hostage.

284
00:15:58,380 --> 00:15:59,560
How many suspects are there?

285
00:16:00,060 --> 00:16:03,380
We have no idea about the number of suspects, their weapons,
or anything else about what's going on inside.

286
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:10,260
We can't get anywhere near it like this.

287
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:13,980
If we move carelessly and provoke the suspect,
the hostage could be in danger.

288
00:16:14,760 --> 00:16:16,200
So we can't do a thing

289
00:16:16,200 --> 00:16:18,520
By the way, where's Ryo-chan?

290
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:19,960
Hey, he's here!

291
00:16:20,660 --> 00:16:21,640
Just kidding!

292
00:16:21,640 --> 00:16:22,640
When did he get here?

293
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:23,800
Hey, Ryo-zu!

294
00:16:23,800 --> 00:16:25,460
Yes, what is it, Chief?

295
00:16:25,460 --> 00:16:29,540
This is awkward. Nakagawa,
lower your head a little, would you?

296
00:16:29,540 --> 00:16:32,040
Like this? Is this good enough?

297
00:16:32,560 --> 00:16:34,800
Hey, Ryotsu!
This is no time for fooling around!

298
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:37,880
Now, how are we supposed to find out what's going on inside
without the suspect noticing us?

299
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:40,020
...without the suspect noticing us?

300
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:43,320
So that's the trick.

301
00:16:43,320 --> 00:16:46,000
That's treating people like garbage!
That's cruel, Chief!

302
00:16:46,580 --> 00:16:49,280
Only you can handle this mission.

303
00:16:49,280 --> 00:16:50,660
I don't want to go.

304
00:16:51,180 --> 00:16:52,980
It's to make up for all the slacking you do.

305
00:16:52,980 --> 00:16:56,720
Listen, scout out the situation
inside and report back to us.

306
00:16:56,720 --> 00:16:58,080
Be careful, senpai.

307
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:59,440
Good luck, Ryo-chan.

308
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:01,440
Alright, here we come, you bastards!

309
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:04,220
Let's go, Ryotsu!

310
00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:10,640
You useless piece of crap, you bastard!

311
00:17:32,040 --> 00:17:34,800
Hic, hic, hic, hic

312
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:40,740
Those bastards went and threw pebbles at us.

313
00:17:40,740 --> 00:17:42,540
What a damn fucking joke.

314
00:17:43,140 --> 00:17:46,020
Shit, because you idiots
went and screwed things up,

315
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:48,120
I'm stuck having to do this crap!

316
00:17:48,460 --> 00:17:50,440
I'm definitely going to arrest you bastards,
you hear me?

317
00:17:52,120 --> 00:17:55,520
Two suspects,
around thirty years old, total thugs.

318
00:17:56,080 --> 00:17:59,600
Weapons: an AUG and a Smith & Wesson,
two guns.

319
00:18:00,020 --> 00:18:04,160
Two young male hostages, they seem healthy,
so they can probably hold out another ten hours.

320
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:06,580
Put a floor plan of the room in there too.

321
00:18:06,580 --> 00:18:10,080
We'll disable the weapons,

322
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:14,140
so storm the place in one hour.

323
00:18:14,660 --> 00:18:17,000
But how do we get this note to them?

324
00:18:35,140 --> 00:18:35,900
What is that?

325
00:18:35,900 --> 00:18:37,440
It looks like a ruler, but...

326
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:38,800
What's he going up there for?

327
00:18:38,800 --> 00:18:41,960
Someone's using that to fling something.

328
00:18:45,140 --> 00:18:46,460
No, it wasn't me, I swear!

329
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:48,180
It wasn't me either.

330
00:18:48,180 --> 00:18:48,840
Hey.

331
00:18:49,660 --> 00:18:50,400
Hey!

332
00:18:53,580 --> 00:18:54,500
No abnormalities, sir.

333
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,720
There must be someone in the room.

334
00:18:56,720 --> 00:18:57,420
Search for them!

335
00:18:57,420 --> 00:18:59,740
There shouldn't be anyone
besides the hostages.

336
00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:00,840
That can't be right.

337
00:19:00,840 --> 00:19:01,920
Just search anyway!

338
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:07,880
I don't think there's anyone there, though.

339
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:09,880
Eeeeeeeh!

340
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:17,060
With this, we can see inside, yeah.

341
00:19:20,520 --> 00:19:25,300
Hold it, heh heh. What does it say?
I can't read it, the letters are too small.

342
00:19:26,380 --> 00:19:31,020
Someone bring a microscope!
Is someone hiding in there? Hey.

343
00:19:31,020 --> 00:19:33,020
Hey! If anyone's in there,
you won't get off easy!

344
00:19:34,460 --> 00:19:36,000
Damn, it's stiff, this thing!

345
00:19:36,940 --> 00:19:38,120
Finally got it loose!

346
00:19:41,740 --> 00:19:42,440
Scratch, scratch.

347
00:19:43,220 --> 00:19:44,940
You're cute, you!

348
00:19:45,260 --> 00:19:46,320
Hey, kid!

349
00:19:47,100 --> 00:19:47,460
Yes!

350
00:19:47,620 --> 00:19:49,220
This one's hungry, isn't he?

351
00:19:49,520 --> 00:19:52,120
Yeah, we haven't fed him
anything since this morning.

352
00:19:52,340 --> 00:19:54,440
That's no good! You have to do it properly!

353
00:19:54,960 --> 00:19:57,440
Poor little thing, just wait there, okay!

354
00:19:57,540 --> 00:19:59,080
Now, let's get some food in him!

355
00:20:01,220 --> 00:20:03,060
Hey, looks like I'm
going to get some food too.

356
00:20:03,320 --> 00:20:05,000
Phew, saved.

357
00:20:15,580 --> 00:20:16,660
Isn't there any food for me?!

358
00:20:16,780 --> 00:20:18,220
Sorry, there's nothing at all.

359
00:20:18,220 --> 00:20:21,260
What?! I'm not even tasty to eat!

360
00:20:21,580 --> 00:20:23,840
Wait, the food's coming now!

361
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,740
What a naughty little one, aren't you?

362
00:20:25,740 --> 00:20:27,080
Did you go out outside, did you?

363
00:20:27,080 --> 00:20:30,260
There you go,
it's got that cabbage feel, see?

364
00:20:30,260 --> 00:20:32,320
Is it tasty

365
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:33,140
Hehehe.

366
00:20:33,140 --> 00:20:33,680
Nom nom.

367
00:20:36,460 --> 00:20:38,280
One leaf is enough to fill your tummy.

368
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:40,560
Well, let's put the rest
away for stir-frying, okay?

369
00:21:11,040 --> 00:21:14,760
Storm in after one hour!

370
00:21:14,760 --> 00:21:15,360
What?

371
00:21:16,780 --> 00:21:20,260
It's been an hour since Ryo-chan went in,
so we have about 10 minutes left.

372
00:21:21,420 --> 00:21:25,360
It's worrying to trust Ryotsu's orders,
but we're getting nowhere like this.

373
00:21:25,360 --> 00:21:27,740
We have no choice but to bet on
a one-in-a-hundred-million chance.

374
00:21:28,100 --> 00:21:30,200
Listen, we're going in in 10 minutes.

375
00:21:38,420 --> 00:21:40,140
You're still hungry?

376
00:21:40,880 --> 00:21:41,460
Hang on there, okay?

377
00:21:43,300 --> 00:21:45,240
Phew, that was a relief!

378
00:21:46,420 --> 00:21:48,820
Hey, this is bad, something's wrong outside.

379
00:21:49,680 --> 00:21:51,780
Damn, an hour has already passed?

380
00:21:51,780 --> 00:21:54,660
We need to remove that
gun's firing pin quickly.

381
00:21:55,480 --> 00:21:57,560
Go on, come on, go!

382
00:21:58,280 --> 00:21:59,180
Ugh, come on.

383
00:21:59,180 --> 00:22:00,820
Damn it, ugh!

384
00:22:00,820 --> 00:22:02,460
Yabu!

385
00:22:02,460 --> 00:22:05,900
Stop your useless resistance.
Your guns are out of commission.

386
00:22:05,900 --> 00:22:07,580
R-really, it's true!

387
00:22:07,580 --> 00:22:09,460
Come on, give up already.

388
00:22:11,880 --> 00:22:15,600
Fine. I guess trusting Ryotsu
was a mistake after all.

389
00:22:16,020 --> 00:22:17,940
Come on, go, go, hup!

390
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:22,560
Should we fall back for now?

391
00:22:22,560 --> 00:22:23,840
Leave the hostages to you, Nakagawa.

392
00:22:23,840 --> 00:22:24,200
Chief.

393
00:22:24,740 --> 00:22:26,580
You can't be a cop if you're scared of guns!

394
00:22:28,520 --> 00:22:29,160
Move!

395
00:22:44,020 --> 00:22:44,740
I've done it!

396
00:22:45,660 --> 00:22:46,900
It's a big sister!

397
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:48,300
That was scary!

398
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:49,580
There, there, little one!

399
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:52,180
Chief, are you hurt?

400
00:22:52,540 --> 00:22:54,900
See, with enough fighting spirit,
anything can be done!

401
00:22:54,980 --> 00:22:55,980
Just as expected of the Chief!

402
00:22:56,240 --> 00:22:57,920
By the way, where's Ryo-chan?

403
00:22:58,600 --> 00:23:01,060
In this situation,
he might have been trampled.

404
00:23:01,060 --> 00:23:04,820
What fighting spirit!
I risked my own neck to save you!

405
00:23:06,160 --> 00:23:07,880
How about that, Ryo-skan Knight!

406
00:23:08,060 --> 00:23:11,280
You should have learned, right down to your bones,
how small your existence is!

407
00:23:11,500 --> 00:23:12,520
Damn you!

408
00:23:13,880 --> 00:23:15,320
Absolutely, thoroughly.

409
00:23:15,700 --> 00:23:17,780
So, I'll reflect on my past conduct

410
00:23:17,780 --> 00:23:19,700
and go on living with a humble
heart from now on, right?

411
00:23:19,700 --> 00:23:21,980
Yes, I've completely reformed myself.

412
00:23:21,980 --> 00:23:26,900
I deeply, deeply regret
everything I've done until now.

413
00:23:27,440 --> 00:23:30,380
Hahaha, good, good, there there.

414
00:23:30,380 --> 00:23:33,460
Well then, it's about time I
returned you to your original form.

415
00:23:33,460 --> 00:23:36,180
Divine punishment, bazaaa-kyaa!

416
00:23:38,500 --> 00:23:39,060
Ter -

417
00:23:43,980 --> 00:23:44,500
Rose!

418
00:23:45,580 --> 00:23:47,920
Thank goodness! You're back to normal!

419
00:23:48,500 --> 00:23:48,660
Yeah!

420
00:23:48,920 --> 00:23:51,700
Give me back my cane! Without it, I'm...

421
00:23:51,700 --> 00:23:52,680
Go sneeze up your nose!

422
00:23:53,660 --> 00:23:56,040
Sakamoto! Feel how small you really are!

423
00:23:56,140 --> 00:23:58,680
You damned fool! Help me!

424
00:24:15,340 --> 00:24:23,660
Surprise and commotion, solved in
the nick of time, quick to lend a hand

425
00:24:26,360 --> 00:24:35,300
Decided, bursting with inspiration, bouncing
along, gathered up and flying into action

426
00:24:36,220 --> 00:24:39,920
Above all, an amazing power

427
00:24:39,920 --> 00:24:46,040
Everyone gather, come here

428
00:24:46,040 --> 00:24:52,320
Like a dream, the final energy

429
00:24:53,180 --> 00:24:56,720
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday

430
00:24:56,720 --> 00:24:59,620
Drawing the universe, standing on the earth

431
00:24:59,620 --> 00:25:03,340
Kameari's star spins around,
and that's how it goes

432
00:25:05,840 --> 00:25:07,060
This should be fine, right?

433
00:25:07,060 --> 00:25:08,600
Of course it's not fine!

434
00:25:21,100 --> 00:25:22,120
What is this, Tobo-robo?

435
00:25:22,120 --> 00:25:24,720
Maria's sister Marilyn
fell for you at first sight?

436
00:25:24,980 --> 00:25:28,120
But you've got a fiancée named Jodie!

437
00:25:29,620 --> 00:25:32,740
And you double-booked your dates on your birthday,
of all days!

438
00:25:33,380 --> 00:25:35,360
Next time: the hellish double date!

439
00:25:35,620 --> 00:25:37,280
You're so popular, Volvo-kun!

